   identifier of each if-gate, innermost first, as a SOPS key. As one compound condition it
   read the set token and reported this tile "declared, not live" for as long as the producer
   stays disarmed. Innermost, the flag reads as an undeclared key and the absence is excused.
   Drop this inner gate in the PR that arms the producer (#2587): armed, the excuse would hide
   a tile that failed to appear. #}
{% if render_records_push_token | default('') %}
{% if render_records_enabled | default(false) | bool %}
  render-records.json: |
    {"type": "push", "name": "k8s Render Records", "description": "The hourly kuma-check-render-records timer on daniel-box dry-runs every renderable k8s service at the newest green origin/master commit and writes /var/lib/homelab/k8s-renders.d, which probe.py releases --stale-only reads. DOWN names the services whose record was not refreshed; a missing beat means the producer stopped or keeps deferring on a pending CI walk. journalctl -u kuma-check-render-records on daniel-box.", "interval": {{ render_records_push_interval_s }}, "max_retries": 0, "resendInterval": {{ kuma_push_resend_down_beats }}, "push_token": "{{ render_records_push_token }}", "notification_name_list": ["{{ kuma_notification_id }}"]}
